Project 2: Innovation Dashboard – Compare online vs. offline sales
Key Insights
1. Revenue by Country:
• The United States generates the majority of total revenue (about $25M of $35.64M), and almost all of it is offline.
• Australia and Germany stand out because online sales make up a huge chunk of their total country sales compared to others.
• Why it matters: The US is the core market, but its online channel looks underdeveloped.
• Recommendation: The US is the biggest market but almost entirely offline, so even a small increase in its online share would add a lot of revenue. Prioritize online marketing and promotions in the US, starting with the categories that already sell well online Accessories and Clothing.
2. Sales & Order Volume Trend:
• Sales and order volume are higher in 2014 months than in the same months of 2013, but the 2014 data stops halfway through the year (June), so full-year totals can’t be compared directly.  
3. Category Breakdown:
• Components generate the highest offline revenue around $22M but register zero online revenue.
• Accessories and Clothing bring in the most online orders and customers.
• Why it matters: Online sales rely on smaller, easy-to-ship products, while components are likely sold to stores and business customers.
• Recommendation: Test whether components could be sold online, and promote accessories and clothing as add ons to bike purchases.
4. Repeat Customers:
•  Online has more repeat customers in total than offline (938 vs 360).

Data Model explanation:
1. Sales Information: 
• SalesOrderHeader and SalesOrderDetail are linked together and cross filter is set to single so the filters flow correctly. 
• SalesOrderHeader holds overall order dates, totals, and customer IDs
• SalesOrderDetail holds number of items sold and product links.
2. Product Information: 
• Tables are linked from Product to ProductSubcategory to ProductCategory.
• This is done so we can analyze the product categories.
3. Customers Information:
• The Customer table is linked to both the Person and Store tables. 
• This is done to separate individual online customers from wholesale business customers.
4. Country Information:
• SalesTerritory links to CountryRegion to get data about countries and territories.
